## Swagger / OpenAPI 3.0 Requirements

Every endpoint MUST have a Swagger doc block. Location: `src/docs/openapi.yaml`

### Required Swagger Fields Per Endpoint

```yaml
/api/vehicles:
  get:
    summary: List all vehicles with current state
    description: Returns all registered vehicles joined with their latest telemetry state. Used for the fleet overview page.
    tags: [Vehicles]
    security:
      - bearerAuth: []
    parameters:
      - name: status
        in: query
        schema:
          type: string
          enum: [active, inactive, maintenance, all]
          default: all
      - name: deviceStatus
        in: query
        schema:
          type: string
          enum: [online, stale, offline, all]
          default: all
    responses:
      '200':
        description: List of vehicles with current state
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/VehicleListResponse'
            example:
              success: true
              count: 2
              vehicles:
                - vehicleId: "V001"
                  label: "Truck Alpha"
      '401':
        $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
      '500':
        $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'
```

### Swagger Component Schemas (define once, reference everywhere)

Define these in `components/schemas`:
- `Vehicle` — full vehicle object
- `VehicleCurrentState` — live telemetry state object
- `TelemetryPayload` — hardware input payload
- `Alert` — alert object
- `Trip` — trip object
- `Driver` — driver object
- `Device` — device object
- `DriverViolation` — violation record
- `ErrorResponse` — standard error shape `{ success, error: { code, message } }`
- `VehicleListResponse`, `VehicleDetailResponse`, etc.

### Swagger Setup

```javascript
// src/app.js
const swaggerUi = require('swagger-ui-express');
const YAML = require('yamljs');
const swaggerDoc = YAML.load('./src/docs/openapi.yaml');

app.use('/api/docs', swaggerUi.serve, swaggerUi.setup(swaggerDoc));
```

Swagger UI accessible at: `http://localhost:3000/api/docs`

---

## Pagination Pattern

All list endpoints that return collections support pagination:

```javascript
// Standard query params
const limit = parseInt(req.query.limit) || 50;   // max 200
const offset = parseInt(req.query.offset) || 0;

// Standard response shape
{
  success: true,
  total: 1440,      // total records matching filter
  count: 50,        // records in this response
  offset: 0,
  records: [...]
}
```

---

## Query Parameter Defaults

| Endpoint | Parameter | Default |
|---|---|---|
| GET /api/vehicles | status | all |
| GET /api/vehicles | deviceStatus | all |
| GET /api/vehicles/:id/history | from | 24 hours ago |
| GET /api/vehicles/:id/history | to | now |
| GET /api/vehicles/:id/history | limit | 200 |
| GET /api/vehicles/:id/trips | from | 7 days ago |
| GET /api/vehicles/:id/trips | status | all |
| GET /api/vehicles/:id/trips | limit | 50 |
| GET /api/vehicles/:id/alerts | status | open |
| GET /api/vehicles/:id/alerts | severity | all |
| GET /api/drivers/:id/violations | from | 30 days ago |
| GET /api/alerts | status | open |

---

## Middleware Application Rules

```javascript
// Auth levels — applied at route registration level
router.get('/',         authMiddleware, handler);          // JWT required
router.post('/login',                  handler);           // No auth (login)
router.post('/telemetry', deviceAuthMiddleware, handler);  // Device token only
```

Never apply both `authMiddleware` and `deviceAuthMiddleware` to the same route.

---

## WebSocket Event Design Rules

All WebSocket messages use the envelope:
```javascript
{
  type:      string,   // SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE constant
  payload:   object,   // event-specific data
  timestamp: string    // ISO 8601 UTC, always server-added
}
```

Rules:
1. `type` strings are SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE
2. `timestamp` is always added by the server, never by hardware
3. `payload` is always an object, never a primitive
4. Every event type must be documented in `docs/FuelGuard_Backend_Spec.md` Section 4
5. Existing event types cannot be renamed without a breaking change discussion

---

## New Endpoint PR Checklist

- [ ] Route added to `src/routes/<resource>.js`
- [ ] Route registered in `src/app.js`
- [ ] Zod validator created in `src/validators/`
- [ ] Service function created in `src/services/`
- [ ] Repository function created in `src/db/repositories/`
- [ ] Swagger YAML block added for the endpoint
- [ ] All response shapes match `docs/FuelGuard_Backend_Spec.md`
- [ ] All error codes are from Section 8 of the spec
- [ ] Unit tests written for service layer
- [ ] Integration test written for the route
- [ ] Smoke test written for happy path